# Netlify redirect rules, shipped INSIDE the publish directory.
#
# These duplicate netlify.toml's [[redirects]] on purpose. netlify.toml is read
# when Netlify BUILDS the site; it is not consulted for a deploy that uploads a
# prebuilt directory through the API. This project deploys that way — the repo
# is not the deploy source — so rules that live only in the toml simply do not
# exist on the live site.
#
# The consequence was not subtle: without the SPA fallback below, every route
# except "/" returned 404. Refreshing on /tasks, following a bookmark, or
# arriving at /oauthredirect after signing in with Zoho all failed, while the
# home page looked perfectly healthy.
#
# Order matters — the first match wins, so the catch-all must come last.

# The calendar feed is proxied so subscribers see an iih.ng URL rather than a
# Convex one, and so the origin can change without every subscription breaking.
/api/calendar-ics  https://your-prod-deployment.eu-west-1.convex.site/calendar.ics  200!

# SPA fallback. Every unmatched path serves the app shell and React Router
# decides from there. Status 200, not 302: the browser must keep the requested
# URL, or the router has nothing to route on.
/*  /index.html  200
